📘 Introduction

In verification, *coverage* measures how much of the **design and functionality** has been tested.   It answers:  
> "Have we tested enough to sign off the design?"

There are two types:
- **Code Coverage:** How much RTL was executed.
- **Functional Coverage:** How much functionality was verified.

---
🔹 1️⃣ Code Coverage
Code coverage is automatically collected by simulators.

| Type | Description |
|------|--------------|
| **Line/Block** | How many lines executed |
| **Expression** | All input combinations tested |
| **FSM** | All states and transitions visited |
| **Toggle** | All bits toggled from 0→1→0 |

⚠️ Code coverage shows *what was executed*, not *whether it was correct*.

---

🔹 2️⃣ Functional Coverage
Functional coverage is **user-defined** — written using `covergroup`, `coverpoint`, and bins.

It checks:
- Have we exercised all design **features**?
- Have all **data combinations and transitions** occurred?

Example:
covergroup cg @(posedge clk);
  cp_mode : coverpoint mode;
endgroup
cg cov = new();
✅ Captures all possible values of mode on each clock edge.
---

🔹 3️⃣ Covergroup
A covergroup defines a coverage model and sampling event.

covergroup cg @(posedge clk);
  <coverpoints>
  <cross coverage>
endgroup

Example:
covergroup cg @(posedge clk);
  cp_mode : coverpoint mode;
  cp_en   : coverpoint enable;
  cross cp_mode, cp_en;
endgroup
✅ Samples at every posedge of clk.
---

🔹 4️⃣ Coverpoint & Bins
A coverpoint tracks values of a variable/expression.

covergroup cg @(posedge clk);
  cp_data : coverpoint data {
    bins zero  = {0};
    bins mid   = {[1:254]};
    bins full  = {255};
  }
endgroup
Term	            Meaning
Bins	          Ranges or values you want to count
Hit count	      How many times each bin occurred

➡️ If you skip bin definitions, SystemVerilog auto-creates bins for small types.
---

🔹 5️⃣ Transition Bins
Track how a signal changes between clock cycles.

covergroup cg @(posedge clk);
  cp_data : coverpoint data {
    bins up   = (0 => 1);
    bins down = (1 => 0);
    bins seq  = (0 => 1 => 2);
  }
endgroup
✅ Example use: FSM transitions, handshake signals.
---

🔹 6️⃣ Cross Coverage
Cross coverage tracks combinations of coverpoints.

covergroup cg @(posedge clk);
  cp_mode : coverpoint mode;
  cp_en   : coverpoint enable;
  cross_mode_en : cross cp_mode, cp_en;
endgroup
If mode has 4 bins and enable has 2 bins → 8 combinations.
---

➕ Advanced Constructs
Construct	                                       Description	                                                  Example
iff	                                            Condition for sampling	                           cp_mode : coverpoint mode iff (reset_n);
binsof	                                        Refers to bins from another coverpoint	           bins combo = binsof(cp1.high);
intersect	                                      Select subset of bins by value range	             binsof(cp1) intersect {[10:20]};
ignore_bins	                                    Exclude certain values                           	ignore_bins bad = binsof(cp1.low);
illegal_bins	                                  Mark invalid combinations	                         illegal_bins err = binsof(cp2.high);
---

🔹 7️⃣ Coverage Methods
Coverage objects have methods to control and query data.

Method	                   Description
.sample()	               Manually sample
.get_inst_coverage()   	Get instance coverage %
.start() / .stop()       	Enable/disable
.set_inst_name()	        Rename for reports


Example:

cg cov = new();
always @(posedge clk) cov.sample();
$display("Coverage = %0.2f%%", cov.get_inst_coverage());
---

🔹 8️⃣ System Tasks & Functions
Used to manage coverage globally in simulation.

Task	                                       Purpose
$get_coverage()	                          Overall coverage %
$coverage_save("file.ucdb")             	Save coverage DB
$set_coverage_db_name("file.ucdb")	       Set DB name
$coverage_control("toggle","off")	         Enable/disable specific coverage types


Example:
initial begin
  $set_coverage_db_name("func_cov.ucdb");
  #100;
  $display("Total Coverage = %0.2f%%", $get_coverage());
  $coverage_save("func_cov.ucdb");
end
---

🔹 9️⃣ Coverage Options
Fine-tune coverage model using option.

Option                        	Meaning	                        Example
option.goal               	Target percentage	                  option.goal = 90;
option.at_least            	Minimum hits per bin              	option.at_least = 2;
option.per_instance	         Track per instance                	option.per_instance = 1;
option.weight             	Weighted importance	                option.weight = 2;
option.auto_bin_max	        Limit auto-created bins	            option.auto_bin_max = 16;

Example:
covergroup cg @(posedge clk);
  option.goal = 90;
  option.at_least = 2;
  option.auto_bin_max = 8;
  cp_data : coverpoint data;
endgroup
---

🔹 🔟 Complete Example
module tb;
  logic clk = 0;
  logic [3:0] mode;
  logic enable;

  always #5 clk = ~clk;

  covergroup cg_mode_en @(posedge clk);
    option.goal = 90;

    cp_mode : coverpoint mode {
      bins low  = {[0:1]};
      bins high = {[2:3]};
      bins trans = (0 => 1), (1 => 2);
    }

    cp_en : coverpoint enable {
      bins on  = {1};
      bins off = {0};
    }

    cross_mode_en : cross cp_mode, cp_en;
  endgroup

  cg_mode_en cov = new();

  initial begin
    repeat (10) begin
      mode   = $urandom_range(0,3);
      enable = $urandom_range(0,1);
      @(posedge clk);
    end

    $display("Coverage = %0.2f%%", cov.get_inst_coverage());
    $coverage_save("mode_en_cov.ucdb");
    #10 $finish;
  end
endmodule

✅ Captures:
Value ranges of mode
Transitions of mode
Enable ON/OFF states
All cross combinations
